\b 8. Deploy Prometheus and Grafana\b0\par
\f1 kubectl apply -f k8s/monitoring/01-prometheus.yaml\par
kubectl apply -f k8s/monitoring/02-grafana.yaml\par
kubectl rollout status deployment/prometheus -n taskflow --timeout=180s\par
kubectl rollout status deployment/grafana -n taskflow --timeout=180s\par
\f0\par
Prometheus discovers the three TaskFlow services through Kubernetes DNS names and scrapes the \f1 /metrics\f0 path every 15 seconds. Grafana is preconfigured with Prometheus as its default data source.\par
\par
\b 9. Deploy ELK and Filebeat\b0\par
\f1 kubectl apply -f k8s/logging/03-elk.yaml\par
kubectl apply -f k8s/logging/04-filebeat.yaml\par
kubectl rollout status deployment/elasticsearch -n taskflow --timeout=300s\par
kubectl rollout status deployment/logstash -n taskflow --timeout=300s\par
kubectl rollout status deployment/kibana -n taskflow --timeout=300s\par
kubectl rollout status daemonset/filebeat -n taskflow --timeout=300s\par
\f0\par
Logstash uses a reduced JVM heap for Docker Desktop:\par
\f1 LS_JAVA_OPTS=-Xms256m -Xmx256m\par
\f0\par
This avoids Logstash being OOM-killed in a local Kubernetes cluster.\par
